+# To-do app
+
+A single static page (`index.html` + `app.js`), no build step or server. Open `index.html` directly in a browser.
+
+## Behavior
+
+- Add a task; input is trimmed and blank input is rejected with "Enter a task."
+- Check/uncheck to mark complete/incomplete; Delete removes one task.
+- Tasks persist in `localStorage` under `todo.tasks.v1` as `[{ id, text, done }]`. Unparseable or malformed data loads as an empty list. Storage is per browser and per origin: opening the file from a different path or a server gives a separate list.
+
+## Tests
+
+`pnpm install && pnpm exec playwright install chromium && pnpm test` runs Playwright E2E tests (`tests/todo.spec.js`) on desktop and mobile Chromium viewports. Tests serve repo files through `page.route` under a fixed `http://localhost:4173` origin and abort every other request, so no server or network is needed. CI runs the same command (`.github/workflows/test.yml`).
+
+## Verification notes (2026-09-23)
+
+- 16/16 tests pass locally (8 tests × desktop/mobile).
+- Mutation checks: disabling `saveTasks` fails the persistence tests; removing `trim()` fails the add/blank tests.
+- Opened via `file://` in Chromium: tasks and completion state survive reload.
+- Desktop (1280×720) and mobile (Pixel 7) screenshots checked: content above the fold, long text wraps, 44px tap targets.
+- Not checked: Firefox/Safari, and the CI workflow (no GitHub remote yet).
